# WHAT THE WEBSITE IS, AS OPPOSED TO WHAT THE REPOSITORY IS.
#
# Every file in this repo was being served as part of the site: /CLAUDE.md,
# /scripts/build-scheme.js, /tests/csp.test.js and /.github/workflows/*.yml all
# returned 200. Nothing secret is in them and the repo is public, so this
# disclosed nothing — but it is the day the repo goes private that it would,
# silently, because the deployment would go on serving what the repository had
# stopped sharing. A deployment should carry what the site needs and nothing
# else.
#
# WHAT STAYS, and why each one has to:
#   index.html + the section shells   the site
#   assets/                           styles and scripts
#   data/                             fetched by the browser AND required by
#                                     api/_lib/retrieve.js at request time
#   api/                              the answer engine
#   sitemap.xml robots.txt og-image.png vercel.json
#
# Verified after deploying, not assumed: the docs are clear that Vercel's own
# default ignore list is a CLI concept, so whether this file reaches a
# Git-connected deployment is a question to answer with a request rather than a
# reading. If /scripts/build-scheme.js still answers 200, the fallback is a
# redirect rule in vercel.json, which is evaluated ahead of the filesystem.

scripts/
tests/
.github/
CLAUDE.md
